  "stress_screen_note": "live control on the 3x gate's own resolving power: each repeat is preceded by a render of an RNG-using preset in the same process. `lapharp` is the counter-example -- it passes a 3x gate most of the time and is still bimodal on the wet bus while its all-off dry bus is stable, so a single 3x PASS is weaker evidence than it looks and is NOT, by itself, a determinism claim. The three issue-named carriers are included so their REFUSAL is characterised rather than merely asserted: a carrier whose ALL-OFF DRY bus is already unstable is nondeterministic in the voice path, upstream of every FX slot, which is a property of the preset and not of fx:Reverb 2.",
